# Branch names

When creating a git branch, use one of these prefixes and kebab-case after the slash. Never `cursor/` and never an unprefixed name.

- `feature/` — new behavior
- `refactor/` — structure or clarity, no intended behavior change
- `fix/` — bug that is not an urgent production break
- `hotfix/` — urgent production fix
- `chore/` — tooling, deps, CI, formatting

Examples: `feature/search-language-filter`, `refactor/extract-named-config-objects`, `hotfix/rate-limit-crash`.

